          "final_text_tail": "The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what was added to `src/jinja2/ext.py`:\n\n1. **`ConditionalI18nExtension` class** (line 574) with:\n   - `tags = {\"ctrans\"}` to register the template tag\n   - `parse()` method that parses the condition expression, optional variables/trimming modifiers, singular content block, optional `pluralize` block, and mandatory `fallback` block\n   - `_parse_block()` method that parses block content until `endctrans`, `pluralize`, or `fallback`\n   - `_trim_whitespace()` method using the same regex as the standard `trans` tag\n   - `_make_conditional_node()` method that creates an `If` node with the condition as test, translation path (gettext/ngettext) in the body, and fallback rendering in the else branch\n\n2. **Module-level alias** `conditional_i18n = ConditionalI18nExtension` (line 1118)\n\nKey behaviors:\n- Commas are optional separators in the header\n- `trimmed`/`notrimmed` applies to all blocks including fallback\n- `TemplateSyntaxError` for missing fallback (\"expected 'fallback' block\") and unclosed blocks (\"unclosed conditional translation block\")\n- `TemplateAssertionError` for duplicate variables (\"defined twice\")\n- Supports both old-style (`Mod` node) and new-style (keyword arguments) gettext formatting\n- `MarkSafeIfAutoescape` wrapping for proper autoescape behavior",
